35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It seems we have some challenges ahead. I found that hazardous materials in older blocks have caused significant delays, and outdoor work has been heavily impacted by rain and frost. We must be very careful with our timing.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"That's worrying, Shizue! I found that our specialist rooms are often empty, while people are constantly being turned away from general rooms. Also, taking rooms out of service has been really expensive because we've had to hire outside space!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,"My findings are concerning. Our bench technicians are wasting hours on manual tasks because the extraction equipment is outdated. Meanwhile, grounds and front-of-house posts remain unfilled, leaving a shrinking staff to handle the burden.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"My findings suggest a pattern: projects that benefit the wider campus are rated highest, while those focused on a single wing disappoint. Also, projects based on comfort or appeal tend to suffer significant delivery delays.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It appears we are facing a trifecta of financial and operational hurdles. I discovered that mechanical plant costs are rising sharply, while we have neglected to set aside any reserves for replacing our aging audiovisual equipment.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@George, it sounds like your technicians are under quite a bit of pressure. @Benjamin, the lack of reserves for equipment is also worrying. We must choose a project that is realistic and helpful to many.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""George"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"I agree with Shizue! Since general rooms are so in demand and hiring outside space is so expensive, we should really look for a project that gives us more flexible space without causing too much disruption.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Yumi, your point about the cost of hiring outside space is well-taken. However, we cannot ignore the inefficiency of our current equipment. It is a burden on the staff that must be addressed to ensure sustainable operations.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, I understand the staff burden, but we must be cautious. My data shows that projects based on ""appeal"" often slip by a year or more. We need a solution that is both practical and widely beneficial.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"It is a fascinating puzzle. We have rising costs for mechanical plant, a void in our AV reserves, and a history of delays for ""appeal"" projects. We must avoid a costly, delayed vanity project.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"I agree with Benjamin. Given the hazardous materials and weather delays I found, we should be very cautious about any project that involves extensive ground-floor renovations or outdoor work. We need a safe, timely solution.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"Wait, if outdoor work is risky and ground-floor renovations are slow, maybe we should look for something that doesn't involve those? But we really need more general-purpose rooms for everyone!","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"If we want to avoid the risks Shizue mentioned while addressing the staff burden, upgrading the laboratory ventilation seems the most logical. It solves a concrete operational failure and supports our technicians.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, while that helps technicians, my data warns that projects benefiting only a single wing are rated lowest. We should prioritize a project that offers campus-wide utility and a high probability of on-time delivery.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@George, while your logic is sound regarding the staff, we must consider the financial trajectory. Mechanical plant costs are climbing rapidly. A ventilation upgrade might prove far more expensive than the initial paper figures suggest.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"I agree with Benjamin. If mechanical costs are rising and outdoor work is so unpredictable, we must be very careful. Perhaps a project that provides general space without these risks is best.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"I totally agree! If we can find a way to get more general-purpose rooms without the risk of huge delays or expensive outside rentals, that would be the best for everyone!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,George,,"I understand the risks, but we cannot let the staff suffer indefinitely. If we ignore the technicians' manual burdens, we are simply trading one operational failure for another. We must find a balance.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, I sympathize with the staff, but we cannot ignore the data. A project that fails to deliver on time or only benefits a few will be a failure for the whole university. We need a broad-impact solution.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we are caught between operational necessity and strategic risk. While George's concerns are poignant, the data suggests that a narrow focus or a mechanical overhaul could be a fiscal and temporal trap.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
